<article class="env-remark" id="2658A9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2658A9">Remark <span data-tag="2658A9">3.2.2.5</span>.</a> The construction of the mapping simplex is functorial, in the sense that a commutative ladder </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \phi :A^0 \ar [d]^{f_0} &amp;  \ldots \ar [l] \ar [d] &amp;  A^ n \ar [l] \ar [d]^{f_ n} \\ \psi :B^0 &amp;  \ldots \ar [l] &amp;  B^ n \ar [l] } \]
</div>
  <p> induces a map $M(f): M(\phi ) \rightarrow M(\psi )$. Moreover, if each $f_ i$ is a categorical equivalence, then $f$ is a categorical equivalence (this follows by induction on $n$, using the fact that the Joyal model structure is left proper). </p>
</article>